/target
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Hook scratch: subagent and validation logs, regenerated per session.
/memory

# The agent maintains this while it works. Session state, not source.
.emma/tasks/

# Screenshot scratch from agents rendering pages; cwd is this repo even when the
# work is not. Never source.
/.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# Runtime session records from the vendored browser. They name a pid and an
# unauthenticated CDP socket, they are dead the moment the process is, and one
# was committed by accident once already.
.browser-miner/

# Loop-harness session state: local to one run, never shared.
.claude/*.local.md

# Python bytecode from the verification scripts. They import the gate snapshot
# to compute the fingerprint, and an import writes one of these next to it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Windows shell-expansion litter. A tool that wrote to `%SystemDrive%\...` or
# `$env:APPDATA\...` without the variable being expanded creates a directory of
# that literal name in the working directory. `Microsoft/Windows/PowerShell/
# ModuleAnalysisCache`, a 16KB binary cache, reached a commit that way on
# 2026-08-23 and was found by `platform.rs`'s survey listing it as repository
# structure.
%SystemDrive%/
Microsoft/

# The working notes, untracked from 2026-08-30 and kept on disk.
#
# 154 files, 9.4MB: lessons, audits, designs, plans, the parity ledger's
# arguments. They were mined into the owner's vault first -- roughly 4,600
# lines across `operational-lore/emma-lessons`, `projects/emma-design-decisions`
# and `research/agent-harness-prior-art`, with the four mockup PNGs copied to
# `attachments/emma-mockups/` and sha256-verified, since a markdown store
# cannot carry them.
#
# Untracked rather than deleted: they are still the working record on this
# machine, and `notes/` is where roughly twenty agents were told to write. What
# leaves is the *repository's* copy, which is what a public tree would carry.
#
# **This does not remove them from history.** Every one is still readable by
# `git log -p` in any clone; that would need a history rewrite and a force-push.
notes/

# The parity programme's paperwork, untracked from 2026-08-31 and kept on disk.
#
# 833 files, 1.5MB: receipts, run logs, reviewer reports, mutation records and
# captured evidence. Every one is a claim about a tree fingerprint that no
# longer exists -- a receipt is pinned to the commit it was taken against, so
# the whole directory went stale on the next commit and stayed stale. That is
# the reason the programme was halted, and shipping its bookkeeping to a public
# clone would hand a stranger 833 files of it.
#
# `emma verify` reads `verification/parity/ledger.json`, so that command has no
# ledger in a fresh clone and says so rather than pretending.
#
# `verification/scripts/` holds the owner's own tooling and stays on this
# machine. CLAUDE.md used to name one of those scripts; that instruction was
# removed on 2026-09-05 and nothing tracked references the directory now.
verification/

# Drafts about the project rather than the project. Four posts, a drafts file
# and screenshots -- unpublished writing, and nothing here depends on it.
blog/

# Which record wins a disagreement. Addressed to somebody working *on* this
# repository, and `docs/` is addressed to somebody trying to understand Emma.
# The page-writing standard used to sit beside it and is tracked now, at
# `DOCS.md` in the root: thirteen tracked files cited it, so leaving it ignored
# meant every one of those citations pointed at nothing a cloner could open.
docs/AUTHORITY.md

# No images in the repository, by the owner's decision on 2026-09-01. The
# history was rewritten to remove every one that had ever been committed --
# four TUI mockups, a blog screenshot, an accidental PowerShell binary cache --
# along with `notes/`, `verification/` and `blog/`. Re-adding one puts it back
# in a history that was cleaned to be publishable.
#
# `docs/img/emma-session.png` is kept on disk and ignored; it is the session
# screenshot the README used to open with.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
docs/img/
